### Tailwind v4 usage

Always reference tokens via `bg-(--token)`, `text-(--token)`, `border-(--token)`. **Do not hardcode hex in components** — use CSS variables / tokens. Tailwind v4 shorthand `font-mono` is equivalent to `font-(family-name:--font-mono)`; **match whichever form the file already uses**.

## Fonts (next/font/google)

| Variable | Font | Use |
|----------|------|-----|
| `--font-display` / `font-(family-name:--font-display)` | **Fraunces** | Page headings, dashboard titles |
| `--font-sans` / default body | **DM Sans** | Body text, labels, buttons |
| `--font-mono` / `font-(family-name:--font-mono)` | **IBM Plex Mono** | Numbers (tabular-nums), SHAs, durations, mono values |

Numeric metric values must use `font-(family-name:--font-mono) tabular-nums`. Page h1s use `font-(family-name:--font-display)`. Other copy is DM Sans (default).

## Spacing scale

Use Tailwind’s standard scale anchored at 4px. Cadence: `gap-2` inside cards, `gap-4` between cards, `px-5 py-4` stat cards, `px-3 py-2.5` compact list rows, `px-8 py-8` main content area.

## Border radius tier

| Class | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `rounded` (4px) | Bare inline elements only (e.g. code pill inside a sentence) |
| `rounded-md` (6px) | Avoid — not in the tier; migrate to `rounded-lg` |
| `rounded-lg` (8px) | Buttons, tooltips, badges, error banners, warning notices |
| `rounded-xl` (12px) | Cards, modals, panels, stat cards, dialogs — the default container radius |
| `rounded-2xl` (16px) | Prohibited in new code; reserved only for marketing-style hero sections |
| `rounded-full` | Icon-only avatar/chip shapes only; not for action buttons |

## Shadow tier

| Class | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `shadow-sm` | Stat cards, modals, elevated cards — the standard card shadow |
| `shadow-md` | Floating panels (dropdowns, popovers, command menus) |
| `shadow-lg` | Toasts, global overlays |
| `shadow-xl` | Prohibited on cards and modals; only acceptable on full-screen drawers |

Never apply Tailwind's raw shadow scale to a component without consulting this table.

## Focus rings (accessibility requirement)

Every interactive element (input, textarea, select, button, [role="option"], combobox) **must** have a visible focus ring:

```
focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-(--accent)/20
```

- `ring-2` not `ring-1` — the thinner ring fails WCAG 2.2 AA contrast
- `/20` opacity on `--accent`, not `/30`
- Never suppress focus rings with `outline-none` alone

## Established component patterns

### Stat card

```
rounded-xl border border-(--border-hairline) bg-(--bg-elevated) px-5 py-4 shadow-sm
  — metric: font-(family-name:--font-mono) text-3xl font-light tabular-nums
  — label: text-xs font-medium text-(--text-secondary)
  — sub: text-[11px] text-(--text-faint)
```

### Feature / link card (IAM-style)

```
rounded-xl border border-(--border) bg-(--bg-field) p-5
  hover: border-(--accent)/40 bg-(--bg-surface)
  — use `group` + `group-hover:text-(--accent)` on title
```

### Data list row

```
flex items-center gap-3 rounded-lg px-3 py-2.5 transition-colors
  default: hover:bg-(--bg-hover)
  focused: bg-(--accent-muted)
```

### Run card (GitHub Actions)

```
rounded-xl border border-(--border-hairline) bg-(--bg-elevated) p-4
  focused: border-(--accent)/50 ring-2 ring-(--accent)/20 shadow-md
  hover: border-(--border) shadow-sm
```

### Action button variants

| Variant | Class pattern |
|---------|---------------|
| Primary | `bg-(--accent) text-white hover:opacity-90` |
| Default | `border border-(--border) bg-(--bg-surface) text-(--text-secondary) hover:border-(--accent)/50 hover:text-(--accent)` |
| Danger | `border border-(--danger)/20 bg-(--danger)/5 text-(--danger) hover:bg-(--danger)/10` |
| Ghost | `border-transparent text-(--text-muted) hover:bg-(--bg-hover)` |

### Skeleton loading

```
animate-pulse rounded bg-(--bg-muted)
```

Skeletons must appear instantly (under 50ms perceived) — render during initial load rather than showing nothing.

### Status indicators (GitHub Actions)

| State | Color token | Visual |
|-------|-------------|--------|
| in_progress | `--accent` | Spinning SVG circle |
| queued / waiting | `--warn` | Clock SVG |
| success | `--success` | Filled circle + check |
| failure / timed_out | `--danger` | Circle + X |
| cancelled | `--text-muted` | Circle + dash |
| skipped | `--text-faint` | Dashed circle + arrow |

### Pulsing activity dot

```html
<span class="relative flex h-2 w-2">
  <span class="absolute inline-flex h-full w-full animate-ping rounded-full bg-(--accent) opacity-60" />
  <span class="relative inline-flex h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-(--accent)" />
</span>
```

Use for **live** activity (e.g. in-progress runs in sidebar). Never for static state.

### Health / progress bar

```
h-1.5 overflow-hidden rounded-full bg-(--bg-muted)
  inner: h-full rounded-full transition-all duration-500
  — green ≥90%: var(--success) | amber 70–89%: var(--warn) | red under 70%: var(--danger)
```

### Empty state

Center-aligned, 40px SVG in `text-(--text-faint)`, `text-sm font-medium text-(--text-secondary)` title, `text-xs text-(--text-muted)` description. No borders or cards around empty states.

### Keyboard hint strip

```
rounded-xl border border-(--border-hairline) bg-(--bg-elevated) px-5 py-3
  <kbd>: rounded border border-(--border) px-1 py-0.5 font-(family-name:--font-mono) text-[10px]
```

## UX principles

1. **Instant perceived speed** — Skeleton cards in under 50ms; never a blank screen.
2. **Quiet when calm** — Urgency only when something needs attention.
3. **Keyboard-first** — `:focus-visible` ring using `--accent`; arrow-key grids where appropriate.
4. **Progressive disclosure** — Summary → grid → detail.
5. **Optimistic mutations** — Update UI immediately; revert on error.
6. **Smart defaults** — in-progress before failures before settled (priority order).

### Modal / dialog backdrop

`bg-black/40` — always use this exact opacity. `/25` and `/30` are too light; they fail to visually separate the modal from complex backgrounds.

## Smart polling (GitHub data)

| Condition | Interval |
|-----------|----------|
| Any run in_progress or queued | 8s |
| Recent failure (last 2 min) | 15s |
| All settled | 60s |
| Tab not focused | Pause (resume on visibilitychange) |
| After mutation | Immediate + 5s follow-up |

Preload GitHub data at shell level; skeletons until first response; cap server fan-out.

## Sticky filter bar (dense views)

```
sticky top-0 z-10 -mx-8 bg-(--bg-deep)/90 px-8 py-3 backdrop-blur-sm border-b border-(--border-hairline)
```

Pair with URL-synced filters (`useSearchParams`) for shareable views.

## Event badge (workflow trigger)

```
inline-flex rounded-full border border-(--border-subtle) bg-(--bg-muted) px-1.5 py-0.5 font-(family-name:--font-mono) text-[10px] text-(--text-muted)
```

## Active run row — indeterminate progress

Sliding inner bar on `bg-(--bg-muted)` track; pair with live elapsed time, not static text.

## Mutation UX

- **Optimistic** — update immediately; revert on API error.
- **Destructive** — shared `ConfirmDialog`; loading on confirm.

## Server / client boundary

Never import `lib/github/client.ts` or `lib/aws/*` from `"use client"` components. UI uses `/api/*` routes. Pure helpers/types in `lib/github/types.ts` (or similar) are fine.

## Sidebar navigation

**Human-readable overview:** [`/design-system`](../../app/design-system/page.tsx) in the app. **Authoritative detail for implementers** stays in this rule file.

### Structure and registry

- Nav order and modules come from [`lib/modules/registry.ts`](../../lib/modules/registry.ts): `MODULE_NAV`, `SIDEBAR_SERVICE_GROUPS`, optional `SidebarServiceGroup.collapsible` for the AWS shell (hub `headerModuleId` + nested `moduleIds`).
- Do not duplicate link lists in [`components/layout/sidebar.tsx`](../../components/layout/sidebar.tsx) except **icons** and layout specific to the sidebar.

### Visual hierarchy (current product)

- **No** duplicate ALL CAPS tier labels above each block (removed).
- **No** left hairline stripe beside groups (removed).
- Spacing between blocks: `mt-4` after Dashboard / first control row, `mt-6` between major sections.

### Hub rows — service names and vendor marks

- Replace generic “Overview” labels with the **service name** (e.g. AWS hub, GitHub, Fly.io). Collapsible parents use **brand marks** where applicable (Simple Icons paths): **AWS** wordmark fill `#232F3E`, **GitHub** Octocat `fill="currentColor"`, **Fly.io** fill `#7B36F6`. These are **exceptions** to “no raw hex in UI” — reserved for vendor logos only; everything else uses tokens.

### Collapsible AWS section

- First `SIDEBAR_SERVICE_GROUPS` entry uses `collapsible: true`, `headerModuleId: "platforms"` (AWS hub → `/aws`), body `moduleIds`: secrets, amplify, audit, iam.
- Expansion state key for the shell: stable string `aws-section` (not the `/aws` URL).

### Expand all / Collapse all

- Row **at the top of the nav** (above Dashboard): two equal-width controls.

```
flex gap-2
  button: flex-1 min-w-0 rounded-lg border border-(--border-hairline) bg-(--bg-elevated)
    px-2 py-1.5 text-center text-[11px] font-medium text-(--text-secondary)
    hover:bg-(--bg-hover) hover:text-(--text-primary)
```

- Labels: “Expand all” / “Collapse all”.
- Centralized expansion map: `aws-section` plus every collapsible parent **`href`** from `MODULE_NAV` items that define `children` (derived via `listCollapsibleNavParents()`).
- **Expand all** sets every key `true`; **Collapse all** sets every key `false`.
- **Route-driven auto-expand:** when `pathname` matches a section (AWS subtree, secrets, amplify, iam, github, fly, etc.), merge **open** for that key so deep links stay usable (sidebar applies sync in an animation frame after navigation).

### Nav row and chevron (shared pattern)

```
flex items-center gap-2.5 rounded-lg px-2.5 py-2 text-[13px] transition-colors
active: bg-(--accent-muted) text-(--accent) font-medium
inactive: text-(--text-secondary) hover:bg-(--bg-hover) hover:text-(--text-primary)
```

- Nested children under a collapsible: `ml-2.5 pl-2.5` (indent only; no border).
- Chevron button: `w-8 shrink-0`, chevron SVG `14×14`, rotate `-rotate-90` when collapsed.

### Sidebar — activity without noise

Pulsing activity dot ([pattern above](#pulsing-activity-dot)) only when there is **live** GitHub Actions background work (`/github` row); hide when idle.

## Typography scale

| Element | Size | Weight | Font |
|---------|------|--------|------|
| Page h1 | `text-2xl` | `font-medium` | display |
| Section h2 | `text-sm` | `font-semibold` | sans |
| Card title | `text-[13px]` | `font-medium` | sans |
| Body / label | `text-sm` | regular | sans |
| Secondary | `text-xs` | regular | sans |
| Caption / meta | `text-[11px]` | regular | sans |
| Faintest | `text-[10px]` | regular | sans or mono |
| Numeric metric | `text-3xl` | `font-light` | mono |
| Compact numeric | `text-xs` | regular | mono + tabular-nums |

## Accessibility

WCAG 2.2 AA. Visible `:focus-visible` rings (`ring-2 ring-(--accent)/20`). Never rely on color alone — pair with icon or label. Status SVGs need `aria-label`.

## Anti-patterns

- No hardcoded hex in UI code — use `--token`, except **vendor logo fills** in the sidebar brand marks (AWS / Fly.io — see [Sidebar navigation](#sidebar-navigation)).
- No decorative color — pulsing/danger/warn for real state only.
- Empty “all clear” is success, not error.
- No spinners for initial skeleton — use `animate-pulse`.
- Status color always has accessible label.
- `--success` as a primary action color — `--success` is a status/state color (green = healthy). Primary interactive actions always use `--accent`. Use `bg-(--success)` only for success badges, status dots, and health indicators.
- `text-3xl` on page `h1` — page headings are `text-2xl font-medium font-(family-name:--font-display)`. `text-3xl` is oversized.
- `bg-(--bg-field)` on modals and sidebars — `--bg-field` is for form fields and table backgrounds. Modal containers, sidebars, popovers, and header chrome use `--bg-elevated`.
- `rounded-2xl` on standard cards — use `rounded-xl`. `rounded-2xl` is reserved for hero/marketing sections only.
- Non-scale font sizes (`text-[1.05rem]`, `text-[0.9rem]`, etc.) — only use Tailwind’s named scale (`text-xs`, `text-sm`, `text-base`, etc.) or the explicitly documented arbitrary sizes (`text-[13px]`, `text-[11px]`, `text-[10px]`).
- `rounded-md` on buttons — buttons use `rounded-lg`.
- `bg-black/25` or `bg-black/30` as modal scrim — use `bg-black/40`.
